# =============================================================================
# Supabase Edge Functions env vars — copy to `.env.local` (for `supabase start`)
# and configure the production set via the Supabase dashboard → Project Settings
# → Edge Functions → Secrets.
# =============================================================================
#
# NEVER commit real values. `.env*` files (except this example) are git-ignored.
# Dev/staging project vars: see supabase/.env.dev.example → supabase/.env.dev.local
# Setup guide: docs/archive/operations/dev-staging-environment.md
# =============================================================================
#
# Local Google OAuth for `/sign-in` (GoTrue) reads GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET from ui/.env.development — see `ui/.env.example` and
# `scripts/dev/run-with-ui-dev-env.sh` (used by dev.sh / npm run start:supabase).
# =============================================================================


# --- Local prod data sync (optional) ----------------------------------------
# Used by ./scripts/data/sync-prod-public-data-to-local.sh when not exported in the shell.
# Session pooler URI from Dashboard → Connect → Session mode (IPv4-friendly). URL-encode password.
# Copy host + port from the dashboard — do not guess aws-0 vs aws-1 or the region.
# pg_dump needs Session mode (pooler port 5432), not Transaction mode (6543).
# PROD_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# --- Supabase runtime -------------------------------------------------------
# Deployed edge functions: `SUPABASE_URL` + `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` are injected
# by the platform.
#
# Local `./dev.sh` / `supabase start`: same vars are injected into the Docker edge
# runtime — you do **not** need them in `.env.local` for that path.
#
# Local `supabase functions serve --env-file ./supabase/.env.local` only: the CLI **skips**
# SUPABASE_* names in --env-file. `./dev.sh` and `npm run dev:api` run
# `scripts/dev/build-local-functions-env.sh`, which merges `.env.local` with `API_URL` and
# `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` from `supabase status` into `supabase/.temp/functions-serve.env`
# so JWT validation survives function hot reload. If you invoke `functions serve`
# manually, run that script first or export both below under the non-SUPABASE names.
# API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-local-service-role-key-from-supabase-status
#
# (Legacy shell exports — still work on first boot but not after hot reload:)
# SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-local-service-role-key-from-supabase-status
#
# Gmail “Connect Gmail” OAuth redirect_uri must be a URL Google + the browser can open.
# If Edge sets SUPABASE_URL to http://kong:8000, either set this to your public API host
# or rely on the built-in kong→127.0.0.1:54321 fallback in `_shared/gmailMailOAuthAccess.ts`.
# Local Meta inbox: ngrok HTTPS origin for OAuth callback + webhook (Meta rejects http://127.0.0.1).
# `functions serve` strips SUPABASE_* from the edge container — use PUBLIC_API_URL (auto-copied from
# SUPABASE_PUBLIC_URL by scripts/dev/build-local-functions-env.sh) or set PUBLIC_API_URL directly.
# SUPABASE_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-subdomain.ngrok-free.dev
# PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-subdomain.ngrok-free.dev
#
# Read by `_shared/databaseService.ts`, `uploadService`, `get-booked-dates`, etc.


# --- Environment flag ------------------------------------------------------
# Read by `_shared/utils.ts#isDevelopment()`. If either `ENVIRONMENT` or `DENO_ENV`
# equals `development`, certain side effects are softened (e.g. calendar/sheet
# labels, email routing). Deployed functions also check `DENO_DEPLOYMENT_ID` (set
# automatically by Supabase) as a production signal in `submit-form`.
ENVIRONMENT=development
# DENO_ENV=development


# --- Resend (transactional email) -----------------------------------------
# https://resend.com/api-keys — read/write or full-access key.
# Full access required for inbound attachment download (Sending-only → 401 on Receiving API).
RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_me

# Resend Receiving (GAF/pet approval inbound) — see docs/archive/operations/approval-email-inbound.md
# MX on inbound subdomain + webhook for `email.received` → approval-email-webhook.
# RESEND_INBOUND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me
# RESEND_APPROVAL_INBOUND_DOMAIN=inbound.kamehomes.space
# → reply addresses: approvals+{propertySlug}@inbound.kamehomes.space

# Primary "to" address for guest-form notifications.
# Dev default:  sprmke.dev@gmail.com
# Prod default: stlmonaco.theresortresidences@azurenorth.com.ph
EMAIL_TO=sprmke.dev@gmail.com

# Reply-To on most outbound Resend mail. Also the **sole To:** address for
# "New Booking Request" (`sendNewBookingRequestNotify`) after each successful
# public `submit-form` DB save (owners / ops inbox).
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=kamehome.azurenorth@gmail.com


# =============================================================================
# PHASE 3 — admin edge functions + JWT allow list (shipped — mirror into Dashboard secrets for prod)
# =============================================================================
# Set these before deploying `list-bookings`, `transition-booking`,
# `upload-booking-asset`, and `parking-broadcast-email`. See
# `.cursor/rules/admin-auth.mdc` §7, `docs/operations/migration-runbook.md` §11 (production checklist),
# and `docs/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md` §5 (Phase 3).

# Comma-separated Google emails allowed to call admin edge functions.
# Enforced by `_shared/auth.ts#verifyAdminJwt`. Org owners bypass when unset.
# ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS=kamehome.azurenorth@gmail.com

# Platform super-admin (`/admin/*`, serveSuperAdmin). Separate from ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS.
# SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com

# Comma-separated BCC recipients for the parking broadcast email. The initial
# seed list lives in `docs/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md` §6.1 Q4.1 — never hard-code emails
# in source, rotate via env only. **Also editable:** Admin → Settings (`app_settings`).
# PARKING_OWNER_EMAILS=owner1@example.com,owner2@example.com


# =============================================================================
# PHASE 4 — Gmail listener + SD refund cron
# =============================================================================
#
# --- Option A — In-app “Connect Gmail” on /settings (recommended for operators) ---
# Create a separate OAuth 2.0 **Web application** client in Google Cloud (not the
# same client as Supabase Auth sign-in). Authorized redirect URI must be exactly:
#   {SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/google-mail-oauth-callback
# e.g. local: http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/google-mail-oauth-callback
# Full client JSON download:
# GMAIL_API_WEB_CLIENT_JSON='{"web":{"client_id":"...","client_secret":"...","redirect_uris":["http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/google-mail-oauth-callback"]}}'
# 32-byte AES key for encrypting refresh tokens in Postgres (64 hex chars OR base64):
# openssl rand -hex 32
# GMAIL_OAUTH_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_64_hex_chars_here
# Comma-separated SPA origins allowed to start OAuth (must match browser Origin):
# GMAIL_OAUTH_ALLOWED_RETURN_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://localhost:5173
#
# --- Option B — Legacy CLI (`npm run gmail-auth`) ---
# Run `npm run gmail-auth` once (from scripts/integrations/gmail-credentials.json) to
# populate GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_JSON and GMAIL_OAUTH_TOKEN_JSON in supabase/.env.local.
# Both are full JSON strings — NOT individual fields.

# Full OAuth client JSON (contents of scripts/integrations/gmail-credentials.json):
# GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_JSON='{"web":{"client_id":"...","client_secret":"...",...}}'

# Token JSON returned after browser sign-in (contains refresh_token):
# GMAIL_OAUTH_TOKEN_JSON='{"access_token":"...","refresh_token":"...","scope":"...",...}'

# Gmail listener / backfill: when EMAIL_REPLY_TO is set, only approval replies from that
# sender are processed. Leave unset to allow any sender (permissive). Also editable in Settings.
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=kamehome.azurenorth@gmail.com

# Minutes *before* parsed check-out (Asia/Manila) when `sd-refund-cron` may send the
# guest Check-out & SD Refund email (independent of balance settlement) and evaluate
# auto-transition to READY_FOR_CHECKOUT once settlement is complete. Default: 120.
# SD_REFUND_CRON_EMAIL_LEAD_MINUTES=120

# If check-out was more than this many days ago, sd-refund-cron still transitions
# to READY_FOR_CHECKOUT but skips the guest SD form email. Default: 21. Use 0 to never suppress.
# SD_REFUND_CRON_MAX_CHECKOUT_AGE_DAYS=30  # legacy env; use org_settings per org (default 30)

# Deployment-wide guest app origin — used for email links and default payment QR URLs.
# Not configurable per org in admin UI. Legacy org_settings.public_guest_app_origin
# is used only when this env var is unset.
# PUBLIC_GUEST_APP_ORIGIN=https://kamehomes.space
# GCASH_NAME=Arianna Perez
# GCASH_NUMBER=0962 564 7541
# FACEBOOK_REVIEWS_URL=https://www.facebook.com/kamehome.azurenorth/reviews
# INSTAGRAM_URL=
# TIKTOK_URL=
# EMAIL_LOGO_URL=https://kamehomes.space/images/logo.png


# =============================================================================
# Telegram marketing (Settings + cron + submit-form / cancel-booking)
# =============================================================================
# See docs/reference/telegram-marketing-reminders.md
#
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC...   # from @BotFather (no spaces)
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890   # numeric id only; no quotes; supergroups often -100...
# TELEGRAM_CRON_SECRET=long-random   # optional; pg_net must send X-Telegram-Cron-Secret when set

# =============================================================================
# Contract expiry (Unit handoff Phase B)
# =============================================================================
# CONTRACT_EXPIRY_CRON_SECRET=long-random  # optional; X-Contract-Expiry-Cron-Secret
#   Setup: supabase/snippets/contract-expiry-cron.sql


# =============================================================================
# Telegram staff/cleaner notifications (Settings + cron)
# =============================================================================
# Daily booking summary to staff/cleaner Telegram group.
# Uses a separate chat id (different group) but can reuse the same bot token.
#
# TELEGRAM_STAFF_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC...   # optional; falls back to TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
# TELEGRAM_STAFF_CHAT_ID=-1009876543210   # numeric id for staff group; required for staff sends
# TELEGRAM_STAFF_CRON_SECRET=<openssl rand -hex 32>   # optional; must match Vault telegram_staff_cron_secret
#   Generate:  openssl rand -hex 32
#   Setup:     supabase/snippets/telegram-staff-cron.sql

# =============================================================================
# Telegram admin operations alerts (Operations page + hourly cron)
# =============================================================================
# Workflow reminders to a dedicated admin Telegram group (separate from marketing/staff).
#
# TELEGRAM_ADMIN_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC...   # optional; falls back to TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
# TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CHAT_ID=-1001112223333   # numeric id for admin ops group; required for sends
# TELEGRAM_ADMIN_CRON_SECRET=<openssl rand -hex 32>   # optional; must match Vault telegram_admin_cron_secret
#   Setup:     supabase/snippets/telegram-admin-cron.sql


# =============================================================================
# Guest Inbox — Meta (Facebook Messenger + Instagram)
# =============================================================================
# See docs/operations/inbox-e2e-runbook.md for local OAuth, webhook tunnel, and test flow.
# Meta developer app → add Facebook Login for Business + Webhooks products.
#
# App ID + secret from Meta developer dashboard → Settings → Basic.
# META_APP_ID=your_meta_app_id
# META_APP_SECRET=your_meta_app_secret
#
# 32-byte AES key for encrypting Page access tokens in social_channel_connections.
# openssl rand -hex 32
# META_INBOX_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_64_hex_chars_here
#
# Arbitrary string you enter in Meta webhook config (GET verify handshake).
# META_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN=your_random_verify_token
#
# Comma-separated SPA origins allowed after Meta OAuth redirect:
# META_OAUTH_ALLOWED_RETURN_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://localhost:5173
# Marketing Content Studio: append publishing scopes only after Meta app use cases include them (see docs/operations/meta-app-review.md)
# META_OAUTH_EXCLUDE_PUBLISHING_SCOPES=1
# Optional comma-separated extra scopes: META_OAUTH_EXTRA_SCOPES=
#
# Webhook callback URL (Meta dashboard → Webhooks → Page):
#   Local via tunnel:  https://<tunnel-host>/functions/v1/meta-inbox-webhook
#   Staging/prod:      https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/meta-inbox-webhook
# Subscribe fields: messages, message_echoes, messaging_postbacks, message_deliveries,
#   message_reads, feed, comments, live_comments
#
# AI suggest + auto-send (Guest Inbox Automation, receipt validation, marketing captions).
# Gemini keys from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — must start with AIza (Google AI Studio).
# GROQ_API_KEY from https://console.groq.com — must start with gsk_
# GEMINI_API_KEYS=key1,key2
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# --- Marketing Studio video music (optional) --------------------------------
# Free Jamendo API client id — https://devportal.jamendo.com/
# Powers Trending/Search in Video editor (marketing-music). Upload + Link work without it.
# JAMENDO_CLIENT_ID=your_jamendo_client_id
